_:b361_b35 <https://repository.product-passport.ec.europa.eu/core/vocabs/core-vocabulary#resourceTitle> "StaxWall 10 spare part replacement" .
_:b361_b35 <https://repository.product-passport.ec.europa.eu/core/vocabs/core-vocabulary#url> "https://www.amperia.example/staxwall-10/docs/spare-part-replacement.pdf"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
_:b361_b36 <https://repository.product-passport.ec.europa.eu/product/batteries/vocabs/battery-vocabulary#batteryLabelSymbolMeaning> "The crossed-out wheeled bin means the battery must be collected separately from household waste."@en-gb .
_:b361_b36 <https://repository.product-passport.ec.europa.eu/product/batteries/vocabs/battery-vocabulary#batterySubstancesImpact> "Electrolyte and electrode materials can harm soil, water and health if the battery is disposed of improperly or damaged."@en-gb .
_:b361_b36 <https://repository.product-passport.ec.europa.eu/product/batteries/vocabs/battery-vocabulary#endUserRoleInSeparateCollection> "Do not dispose of the battery with household waste; hand it to the installer or a registered collection point."@en-gb .
_:b361_b36 <https://repository.product-passport.ec.europa.eu/product/batteries/vocabs/battery-vocabulary#endUserRoleInWastePrevention> "Use the battery within its rated limits and have faults repaired by an authorised installer to extend its life."@en-gb .
_:b361_b36 <https://repository.product-passport.ec.europa.eu/product/batteries/vocabs/battery-vocabulary#preparationForRepurposingFacilities> "Authorised repurposing partner for second-life storage: Amperia Second Life, Kassel."@en-gb .
_:b361_b36 <https://repository.product-passport.ec.europa.eu/product/batteries/vocabs/battery-vocabulary#preparationForReuseFacilities> "Authorised re-use partner: Amperia Service Centre, Kassel."@en-gb .
_:b361_b36 <https://repository.product-passport.ec.europa.eu/product/batteries/vocabs/battery-vocabulary#separateCollectionPoints> "Registered collection points: https://www.amperia.example/staxwall-10/collection-points"@en-gb .
_:b361_b36 <https://repository.product-passport.ec.europa.eu/product/batteries/vocabs/battery-vocabulary#takeBackCollectionPoints> "Amperia takes the battery back free of charge through its installer network."@en-gb .
_:b361_b36 <https://repository.product-passport.ec.europa.eu/product/batteries/vocabs/battery-vocabulary#wasteBatterySafetyInstructions> "Disconnect, keep the terminals covered, store dry and away from heat; a damaged battery goes in a non-flammable container."@en-gb .
_:b361_b36 <https://repository.product-passport.ec.europa.eu/product/batteries/vocabs/battery-vocabulary#wasteBatteryTreatmentFacilities> "Authorised recycler for lithium iron phosphate batteries: see https://www.amperia.example/staxwall-10/recycling"@en-gb .
